Without dancing around the question like Ralf (because I assume if you
asked the question you don't mind spoilers)....

Note first that I haven't tried this, but Juiblex shouldn't be much
harder to kill in the main dungeon than in Genhennom.  Juiblex can be
dangerous, but if you have a means of curing sickness almost laughably
simple.  You'll want:

Either a potion of extra or full healing, or a spell of Cure Sickness,
or failing those a blessed unicorn horn (which isn't 100%, but will
nearly always work within the time you'll need it to).  In the absence
of these, making sure your prayer timeout's expired is probably a good
idea.

Okay HP if Juiblex hits instead of engulfs, or gets in a digestion
attack.  (Actually, I'm not sure if he CAN hit, but digestion should
be accounted for.)

A wand of digging.

A weapon that does at least 1 HP damage.

You'll also want to be UNBURDENED. Being fast or very fast is also
probably a good idea.  Being engulfed for longer than one game turn
could mean getting repeat-sickened, which drastically cuts down on
your lifespan when sick, in addition to taking extra digestion damage.

When Juiblex engulfs you, you immediately get sickened, meaning you
have to cure the sickness within a few turns or die from it.  But
while engulfed, all "solid" engulfers (other than vortices or air
elementals) can be damaged down to one hit point by zapping a wand of
digging.  Once at one HP, any smack will kill him, then you can use
your potion/spell/prayer/unicorn horn to cure the sickness.  Juiblex
is probably worth a over a thousand experience points (a lot in
Nethack), so you'll probably gain a level.

Assuming you can survive the engulf and are prepared, Juiblex is
probably the easiest demon lord to kill at low level.

